    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are looking for production from the heart of the order today, led by **Kyle Tucker**, who commands our highest score at 70.33. His matchup against Sproat (4.25 xERA) provides a strong environment for output, bolstered by his prime cleanup spot and favorable platoon dynamics. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** remains an essential cornerstone at 67.94; while he faces a slight platoon disadvantage against Keller, his elite underlying metrics and favorable park factors make him a high-floor, high-ceiling play. Meanwhile, **Gunnar Henderson** (64.90) is a critical start today; despite facing a lefty, his speed profile\u2014specifically his ability to exploit favorable delivery windows for stolen bases\u2014keeps his value elevated even against a tough arm like Valdez.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the optimizer today was bypassing **Nolan Schanuel** (53.06) in favor of the higher-upside profiles currently in the lineup. **Schanuel** was the final cut, narrowly missing the cut behind **Miguel Vargas** (57.67), who benefits from a wind-assisted park advantage and a high-leverage spot in the batting order. We are also monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" statuses for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Coby Mayo**, and **Gage Workman**. **Workman** remains the most precarious start of the day at 42.74; if he drops in the order or if weather risk shifts, he is the primary candidate to be pulled for a bench option like **Brayan Rocchio** or **Josh Jung** to preserve our game caps. With **Luis Robert Jr.** still sidelined on the IL, the depth of our bench is being tested, but the current configuration maximizes our exposure to favorable matchups across the board.",
